Z||000010||My7Fieros||09-10-2001||09:08 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by lowfierogt:<BR><B>How can you keep all the Fiero's on the road 7?   They must pay you good being a cop!<BR>I have three fiero's and two are apart.  The other on is my daily driver is falling apart.<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Only 4 of them run, and two of them run like crap. (White GT and silver SE are the "flagships"...daily drivers.)<BR>And yes, they pay pretty good.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><BR>BTW, what with those of you rolling your eyes at AOL? Its ALL that I use. Only people who dont have it mock it. Use it, and youll see how easy it is (compared to others).<P><BR>------------------<BR><FONT SIZE="3"><FONT COLOR="red"><B><I>My 7 Fieros</FONT></FONT></B></I><p>[This message has been edited by My7Fieros (edited 09-10-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000011||Raydar||09-10-2001||10:18 PM||||I used to use AOL. Still have an account but pretty much never use it.<BR>Biggest problem that I had was trying to dial in. Kept getting busy signals. Next biggest problem was getting "punted". (Dropped connection.) <BR>Once I got my Mindspring account, I would connect to AOL over TCP/IP. NEVER got dropped, and it was way faster.<P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"> [RANT] From my point of view (former computer support person), AOL software is the absolute worst. It's not fully de-bugged before it's released. When you install it, it can screw up your existing network connections. <BR>When AOL 5 was released, we had to reformat and re-image quite a few computers at work, because they were so badly hosed.<BR>There were even lawsuits against AOL, because their software screwed up so many computers.<BR>If it hasn't screwed up your 'puter, you're lucky.<BR>[/RANT]<P>Having said all that, it IS easy to use, and places tons of content right at your fingertips. And what a variety of chatrooms!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>This is NOT meant to be a flame. More power to ya'!<P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>Black 88 Formula.<BR>Red 88 Duke coupe. "The Project" <BR>88 Formula parts car. "The Donor"<BR></FONT><p>[This message has been edited by Raydar (edited 09-10-2001).]||||reg||1
